      "problem": "Select the correct options in the truth table below and use this to determine whether $(A∨¬B)⇒(B⇒A)$ is a tautology.\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,A∨¬B\\,$ | $\\,B⇒A\\,$ | $\\,(A∨¬B)⇒(B⇒A)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-3}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-4}} |\n\nAccording to the table, $(A∨¬B)⇒(B⇒A)$ \n{{field-5}}\nalways true. Therefore, it \n{{field-6}} \na tautology.",
